    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="0928" n="920" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg920"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1079</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Consul
                        General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-13">May 13, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear George</hi>: I am enclosing a copy of a letter,
                    with enclosure, which has been addressed to Paul Knabenshue<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d760-f1"/> concerning the activities <pb facs="0929" n="921"
                        xml:id="pg921"/> of Nuri Pasha looking to the effecting of a compromise
                    settlement between the Jews and Arabs of the Palestine question.</p>
                <p>I need hardly repeat that we shall be most interested in your pursuit of this
                    subject.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
